# HomeOrganizer App — Project Context (Always Apply)

## One-liner
A collaborative home inventory/location organizer: users map a home into deeply nested containers (sections) and attach items (with photos) so they can quickly find where things are stored.

## Primary goals
- Make it easy to record **where items are placed** in a home via a **nested container hierarchy**.
- Support **collaboration** (shared projects) with **realtime updates**.
- Provide a **visual navigation canvas** (infinite-ish grid, draw rectangles) + a **details sidebar**.
- Support **image uploads** for items; optional AI suggests labels/descriptions but user is the source of truth.

## Tech stack (fixed)
- Backend: Laravel 12.x
- Mobile: Flutter
- Realtime: WebSockets via Laravel Reverb

## Core domain concepts (use these terms consistently)
- **Project**: a home/workspace (e.g., "Home 1").
- **Member**: a user who has access to a project.
- **Role**: `owner`, `editor`, `viewer`.
- **Section**: a container/location node in a tree (floor/room/cabinet/box/etc.).
- **Item**: a stored object that belongs to exactly one section (its current location).
- **Asset**: uploaded media (photos) attached to an item (and optionally section, if needed later).

## Structure rules (hard requirements)
- Sections form a **tree** (parent-child).
- Must support **very deep nesting** (target: 100+ levels).
- A section has a user-editable **label/name**.
- An item belongs to **exactly one section** at a time.
- Sharing is **per project**, with clear role permissions.

## MVP UI behavior (high-level)
- Provide an **infinite-ish grid/canvas** similar to diagrams-style apps.
- MVP shapes: **rectangles only**.
- Selecting / zooming into a section updates an **interactive sidebar** that shows:
  - child sections
  - items in the selected section
- Canvas is primarily for navigation + spatial mapping; sidebar is for detail CRUD.

## Realtime collaboration expectations
- Realtime should reflect multi-user changes quickly (no manual refresh).
- Events that should broadcast in MVP:
  - section create/update/move/delete
  - item create/update/move/delete
  - membership/role changes (optional if MVP time is tight)

## AI analyzer (optional feature)
- AI can suggest:
  - item label/title
  - short description
- User can **override/correct** AI output at any time.
- Store AI output as **suggestion metadata**, not as authoritative truth.

## Non-goals (avoid inventing these unless explicitly requested)
- Complex diagramming features (many shape types, constraints, snapping, connectors)
- Offline-first sync
- Full asset DAM / advanced inventory accounting (prices, depreciation, barcode scanning)
- Overly complex permission systems beyond owner/editor/viewer

## Implementation guidance for AI coding assistance
- Keep solutions **MVP-first**: minimal tables, minimal API surface, minimal UI complexity.
- Prefer approaches that scale to deep nesting:
  - Tree modeling must not assume shallow depth.
  - Avoid designs that require loading the entire tree for basic operations.
- Do not introduce new major tech (e.g., GraphQL, microservices) unless explicitly asked.
- Do not claim features exist unless they were stated in this document or explicitly added by the user.

## Terminology mapping examples
- "Home" == Project
- "Floor / Room / Cabinet / Box" == Section (different labels, same model)
- "Thing stored" == Item

